Why this exists (explanation, not part of the permission)

The booth can drive Canon cameras over USB through the EDSDK, which is
proprietary. This repository, its public mirror, every CI build and every
GitHub release contain only the project's own wrapper code; with that free
edition each operator obtains the SDK from Canon and installs it on their
own machine ("--install-edsdk"). The edition with camera SDK, offered on the
project website and built outside this repository, additionally carries the
SDK's runtime libraries, unmodified and in object code only, solely for use
with Canon cameras. Those files are not under the AGPL and not covered by
this permission's grant; they come with end-user terms of their own
(CAMERA-SDK-LICENCE.txt). The permission above settles the AGPL side of
running and conveying the booth together with the SDK.
